# DISCRIM (General Description). If TS 8 contains any digit 1 then TS 15
# is passed into TS 24, otherwise TS 16 is passed into TS 24. The contents
# of TS 2, TS 3, TS 4, TS 5, TS 8 are altered.
#
# Outline of operation. TS 8 is transferred to TS 2 and then subtracted
# from zero, passing into the partial sums register TS 4, TS 5. By taking
# out TS 5 we obtain a minor cycle full of digits 1 or of digits 0
# according as there was or was not a digit 1 in TS 8 originally. We then
# form (TS 5 & TS 15) v (-TS 5 & TS 16) by logical operations and pass it
# on to TS 24.
#
# The report gives the description and the outline and no table. This
# table is ours, and follows the outline step for step. TS 6, 9 and 10 are
# altered as well, and TS 6 is left holding what went into TS 24.
DISCRIM
  1   TS 8 - TS 2
  3   SUBTRACT 'A'
  4   TS 5 - TS 6
  5   TS 6 - TS 9
  6   TS 6 - TS 3
  7   TS 15 - TS 10
  9   AND
 10   TS 3 - TS 10
 12   TS 8 - TS 3
 14   NOT
 15   TS 8 - TS 9
 17   TS 16 - TS 10
 19   AND
 20   TS 8 - TS 9
 22   TS 3 - TS 10
 24   OR
 25   TS 8 - TS 24
 27   B, UNBURY
